            "title": "Topological sorting",
            "date_published": "2024-08-30T04:54:15.000Z",
            "content_html": "<h3 id=\"overview\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#overview\">#</a> Overview</h3>\n<p>In computer science, a topological sort or topological ordering of a <strong>directed grapg</strong> is a linear ordering of its vertices. For instance, the vertices of the grapg may represent tasks to be performed, and the edges may represent constraints that one task ust be performed before another; in this application, a topological ordering is just a valid sequence for the tasks.</p>\n<p><strong>A topological ordering is possible if and only if the grapg has no directed cycles</strong>,that is, if it is a directed acyclic graph (DAG).</p>\n<h3 id=\"example\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#example\">#</a> Example</h3>\n<p><img data-src=\"https://hackmd.io/_uploads/HJTxqmVjR.png\" alt=\"image\" /></p>\n<p>This graph has many valid topological sorts,including:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>5,7,3,11,8,2,9,10</li>\n<li>3,5,7,8,11,2,9,10</li>\n<li>3,5,7,8,11,2,10,9</li>\n<li>5,7,3,8,11,2,10,9</li>\n<li>7,5,11,3,10,8,9,2</li>\n<li>5,7,11,2,3,8,9,10</li>\n<li>3,7,8,5,11,10,2,9</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"algorithms\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#algorithms\">#</a> Algorithms</h3>\n<p><strong>Kahn's algorithm</strong></p>\n<p>Time complexity <em>O(V+E)</em>, Space <em>O(V)</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li>convert input data to a directed graph.</li>\n<li>use an array to record the incoming edges of  vertices.</li>\n<li>add the nodes which has no incoming edge into a queue.</li>\n<li>use the queue to traverse the graph.</li>\n<li>repeat 3 and 4 tile the queue is empty.</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>DFS</strong> <em>O(V+E)</em></p>\n<p>Time complexity <em>O(V+E)</em>, Space <em>O(V+E)</em></p>\n<ol>\n<li>convert input data to a directed graph.</li>\n<li>use an array to mark vertices's states, each vertex has three states including initial, temporary and permanent. If we visite a temporary vertex then return false(cycle detect ), if we visite a permanent vertex, then return true. (to avoid repeated traversal)</li>\n<li>add a permanent vertex into the top of a stack.</li>\n<li>repeat 3 and 4 tile all vertices was visited.</li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"problems\"><a class=\"anchor\" href=\"#problems\">#</a> Problems</h2>\n<p><span class=\"exturl\" data-url=\"aHR0cHM6Ly9sZWV0Y29kZS5jb20vcHJvYmxlbXMvY291cnNlLXNjaGVkdWxlL2Rlc2NyaXB0aW9uLz9lbnZUeXBlPXN0dWR5LXBsYW4tdjImYW1wO2VudklkPXRvcC1pbnRlcnZpZXctMTUw\">Course Schedule</span></p>\n<figure class=\"highlight cpp\"><figcaption data-lang=\"C++\"></figcaption><table><tr><td data-num=\"1\"></td><td><pre><span class=\"token comment\">//Kahn's algorithm</span></pre></td></tr><tr><td data-num=\"2\"></td><td><pre><span class=\"token keyword\">class</span> <span class=\"token class-name\">Solution</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">&#123;</span></pre></td></tr><tr><td data-num=\"3\"></td><td><pre><span class=\"token keyword\">public</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span></pre></td></tr><tr><td data-num=\"4\"></td><td><pre>    <span class=\"token keyword\">bool</span> <span class=\"token function\">canFinish</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token keyword\">int</span> numCourses<span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> vector<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>vector<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token keyword\">int</span><span class=\"token operator\">>></span><span class=\"token operator\">&amp;</span> prerequisites<span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">&#123;</span></pre></td></tr><tr><td data-num=\"5\"></td><td><pre>        vector<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token keyword\">int</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>adj<span class=\"token punctuation\">[</span>numCourses<span class=\"token punctuation\">]</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></pre></td></tr><tr><td data-num=\"6\"></td><td><pre>        vector<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token keyword\">int</s